WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:08.133
Coral reefs are some of
the most diverse places

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.801
on the planet.

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:14.681
But it's not easy being a 
small fish on a big reef.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.767
Tiny animals must 
overcome 

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:21.980
huge challenges to keep 
their coral city alive.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.234
For this production we 
have wonderful gadgets

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.278
that we filmed with.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.613
The closed circuit 
rebreather

00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:34.993
is revolutionary for 
filming animal behavior.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.620
All of the gas that 
you're breathing 

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.873
stays contained within 
this one unit,

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.666
and you don't blow 
bubbles anymore.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.461
And the animals are just
so much more

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:45.754
comfortable around you

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:46.838
they're not scared off 

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:48.006
with every single exhale

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:49.174
that you make.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.634
It's just amazing how
much closer you can get

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:52.844
to all of the fish,

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:53.928
and how much 
longer you can

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:54.763
stay down there.

00:00:56.973 --> 00:00:58.433
Today we were 
searching for 

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.143
Peacock Mantis Shrimp.

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:03.605
Which are a colorful
animal that lives in a hole

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.440
that it builds itself 
in a reef.

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:09.444
It looks amazing
on the probe.

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:11.196
You know being actually 
below it

00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:12.447
and like like looking 
up at it.

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:14.824
It's just so encouraging 
to find a really good animal,

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:17.035
and so encouraging to 
start to see the visual.

00:01:17.035 --> 00:01:19.829
These new scopes that 
we're using on the series

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:22.874
Got a cool shot of it
coming out

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:25.210
like looking super 
aggressive, and then...

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:28.046
Just broke my probe,
just like came out

00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:30.507
and just, 
smashed the front of it

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:35.303
Sometimes nature just 
gives you a little...

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:40.892
We witnessed this
absolutely massive

00:01:40.892 --> 00:01:42.393
Crown-of-thorns
outbreak.

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:45.271
But, these tiny little red
crabs live in

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.941
coral colonies and when
a Crown-of-thorns

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:51.486
puts its arm up over
the top of the coral

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:53.863
these tiny little crabs
they nip away at the 

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.657
the tube feet and at the 
spines of the  

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:56.491
Crown-of-thorn.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.619
The Crown-of-thorn
turns around 

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.121
really quickly and starts 
going the other way.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:04.082
So, it was awesome 
actually.

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:06.835
Just seeing these tiny  
little crabs

00:02:06.835 --> 00:02:09.379
defending their home, 
their little coral colony,

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.171
it was amazing!

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:14.259
A diverse community
of tiny creatures,

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:16.636
all playing their part,

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:20.431
keeps coral reefs healthy
and far more resilient

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:22.684
to the many threats 
they face.

00:02:26.928 --> 00:02:28.884
Tiny World

